IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tprai-types`

-- Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK) — GOAL 2: WHAT THE
-- THIRD PARTY CAN RECOVER AND ENFORCE (ss 1(3)-(4), 8, 9, 10, 14).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2010-10.txt.

§ `Goal 2 — recovery and enforcement`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a b MEANS IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- s 1(3) "The third party may bring proceedings to enforce the rights
-- against the insurer without having established the relevant person's
-- liability; but the third party may not enforce those rights without having
-- established that liability." (4): existence and amount established.
@ref s 1(3)-(4)
GIVEN m IS A `Money facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the third party may enforce the transferred rights under` m IF
    m's `the liability is established`

-- s 8 "Where the liability of an insured to a third party is less than the
-- liability of the insurer to the insured (ignoring the effect of section
-- 1), no rights are transferred under that section in respect of the
-- difference." s 10(2): "The insurer is entitled to set off the amount of the
-- insured's liability against the amount of the insurer's own liability to
-- the third party in relation to the transferred rights."
@ref ss 8, 10
@export The amount the third party can recover from the insurer under rights transferred by the Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK): the lesser of the insured's liability to the third party and the insurer's liability to the insured (s 8), less any amount the insurer may set off under s 10, not below nothing. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN m IS A `Money facts`  @desc The insured's liability to the third party, the insurer's liability to the insured, and the insurer's set-off
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount due from the insurer under` m MEANS
    `the greater of` 0
        (    `the lesser of` (m's `the insured's liability to the third party`) (m's `the insurer's liability to the insured`)
       MINUS m's `the insurer's set-off`)

-- s 14(1) "the third party may enforce that liability against the insured
-- only to the extent (if any) that it exceeds the amount recoverable from the
-- insurer by virtue of the transfer." (6) "the amount recoverable from the
-- insurer does not include any amount that the third party is unable to
-- recover as a result of— (a) a shortage of assets on the insurer's part ...
-- or (b) a limit set by the contract of insurance on the fund available".
-- (7) where the third party is eligible for the FSCS, (6)(a) applies only if
-- it has made a claim, and amounts paid or due from the FSCS count as
-- recoverable.
@ref s 14(1), (6)-(7)
GIVEN m IS A `Money facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount recoverable from the insurer for s 14 under` m MEANS
    `the greater of` 0
        (    `the amount due from the insurer under` m
       MINUS insolvencyShortfall
       MINUS m's `shortfall from a fund limit in the contract`)
    WHERE
        insolvencyShortfall MEANS
            IF   m's `eligible for the FSCS`
            THEN IF   m's `an FSCS claim was made`
                 THEN `the greater of` 0 (m's `shortfall from the insurer's own insolvency` MINUS m's `paid or due from the FSCS`)
                 ELSE 0
            ELSE m's `shortfall from the insurer's own insolvency`

@ref s 14(1), (6)-(7)
@export The part of the insured's liability the third party may still enforce against the insured under s 14 of the Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK): the excess of the liability over the amount recoverable from the insurer, where amounts not recoverable because of the insurer's own insolvency (if an FSCS claim was made when eligible, net of FSCS payments) or a fund limit in the contract do not count as recoverable. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN m IS A `Money facts`  @desc The liability, the amounts due from the insurer, and any shortfall, FSCS claim and payment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount still enforceable against the insured under` m MEANS
    `the greater of` 0
        (    m's `the insured's liability to the third party`
       MINUS `the amount recoverable from the insurer for s 14 under` m)

-- s 9(3) "The transferred rights are not subject to a condition requiring the
-- insured to provide information or assistance to the insurer if that
-- condition cannot be fulfilled because the insured is— (a) an individual who
-- has died, (b) a body corporate that has been dissolved, or (c) an
-- unincorporated body, other than a partnership, that has been dissolved."
-- (4) notifying a claim is not information or assistance. (5) "The
-- transferred rights are not subject to a condition requiring the prior
-- discharge by the insured of the insured's liability to the third party."
-- (6) for marine insurance, (5) applies only to death or personal injury.
@ref s 9(3)-(6)
@export Whether a condition in the contract binds the third party's transferred rights under s 9 of the Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK): a condition to provide information or assistance does not, where the insured has died or is a dissolved body corporate or unincorporated body (not a partnership); a condition of prior discharge by the insured does not, except in marine insurance for liabilities other than death or personal injury; other conditions (including notifying a claim) do. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Condition facts`  @desc The kind of condition, the insured, and for prior discharge whether it is marine insurance and a death or personal injury liability
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the condition binds the transferred rights under` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `kind of condition`
    WHEN `to provide information or assistance` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the insured`
        WHEN `a deceased individual` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a body corporate, dissolved` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an unincorporated body other than a partnership, dissolved` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `prior discharge of the liability by the insured` THEN
        c's `marine insurance` AND NOT (c's `liability for death or personal injury`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE
